{"parameters":{"model":"dxn:com.anthropic.model.claude-opus-5.default","stream":true,"tools":[{"name":"eval","description":"Runs code against the workspace and returns whatever that code printed. This is the only tool: every read, every write and every operation happens inside it.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"code":{"type":"string","description":"The program, in the dialect the system prompt describes. Print anything you need to see."}},"required":["code"],"additionalProperties":true}}]},"prompt":{"content":[{"options":{},"role":"system","content":"## Code mode\n\nYou have exactly one tool, `eval`. Its `code` is the body of an `Effect.gen` generator run\nagainst this workspace, so `yield*` is available and you must NOT write the wrapper yourself.\nIt returns whatever the code printed: a value you do not `print` never reaches you. Do not use\n`import` or `require` — the modules below are already in scope.\n\nPrefer one `eval` call that does the whole job — query, inspect, change, print — over a call\nper step. Print the specific values you need to reason about, not whole objects.\n\n### In scope\n\n- `Database`, `Filter`, `Query`, `Obj`, `Ref`, `Type`, `DXN`, `Operation`, `Effect` —\n  the DXOS modules, as a source file would import them.\n- `types` — every registered object type, keyed by typename:\n  `types['example.com/type/Task']`.\n- `print(...values)` — an effect: `yield* print('count', tasks.length)`. Strings go through\n  verbatim, everything else is printed as JSON.\n\n### Reading and writing\n\n```js\nconst tasks = yield* Database.query(Filter.type(types['example.com/type/Task'], { status: 'open' })).run;\nyield* print('open', tasks.length);\n\nObj.update(tasks[0], (task) => { task.status = 'done'; });\n\nconst created = yield* Database.add(Obj.make(types['example.com/type/Task'], { title: 'New', status: 'open' }));\nyield* Database.flush();\nyield* print('created', created.id);\n```\n\n`Obj.update` is synchronous and is the only way to change a stored object. `Database.remove`\ndeletes one. Call `Database.flush()` before printing a final confirmation.\n\n### References\n\nA `Ref<typename>` field takes `Ref.make(obj)` of an object you hold — never an id or a URI\nstring. Create the target first, then the object that points at it:\n\n```js\nconst owner = yield* Database.add(Obj.make(types['example.com/type/Person'], { name: 'Ada' }));\nyield* Database.add(Obj.make(types['example.com/type/Task'], { title: 'Review', status: 'open', owner: Ref.make(owner) }));\n```\n\nRead a reference back with `yield* Database.load(task.owner)`.\n\n### Types\n\nEvery registered type and its fields (`?` marks an optional field). This is the whole schema —\ndo not introspect it further. A `Ref<typename>` field holds a reference to another object, not\nthe object or its id.\n\n- `com.example.type.expando` — \n- `com.example.type.task` — title: string, status: string, priority?: number\n- `org.dxos.type.feed` — name?: string, kind?: string, namespace?: \"data\" | \"trace\", rewindFrom?: string\n- `org.dxos.type.skill` — name: string, description?: string, instructions: object, tools: string[], agentCanEnable?: boolean, mcpServers?: object[], hooks?: object[]\n- `org.dxos.type.instructions` — name?: string, description?: string, input: object, output: object, text: Ref<org.dxos.type.text>, skills: Ref<org.dxos.type.skill>[], objects?: Ref<org.dxos.schema.anyObject>[], commands?: object[]\n- `org.dxos.type.function` — name: string, description?: string, updated?: string, source?: Ref<org.dxos.schema.anyObject>, inputSchema?: object, outputSchema?: object, services?: string[], binding?: string, icon?: string\n- `org.dxos.type.assistant.chat` — name?: string, viewType?: string, remote?: boolean, feed: Ref<org.dxos.type.feed>, instructions?: Ref<org.dxos.type.instructions>, model?: Ref<org.dxos.schema.anyObject>, tasks: Ref<org.dxos.type.task>[]\n- `org.dxos.type.trigger` — runnable?: Ref<org.dxos.type.function>, spec?: object, enabled?: boolean, remote?: boolean, concurrency?: number, inputNodeId?: string, input?: object\n- `org.dxos.type.tag` — label: string, hue?: string\n- `org.dxos.type.alarm` — wakeAt: number, message?: string, created: string\n- `org.dxos.type.view` — query: object, projection: object\n\n### Operations\n\nNo operations are bound to this conversation."},{"options":{},"role":"user","content":"Every task of type com.example.type.task whose title mentions docs must be closed: set its status to \"done\". Then tell me how many tasks are done in total."},{"options":{},"role":"assistant","content":[{"options":{},"type":"text","text":"I'll find the tasks mentioning \"docs\", close them, then count all done tasks."},{"options":{},"type":"tool-call","id":"toolu_01EvQkZjnZybkdPD9rVppr7A","name":"eval","params":{"code":"const all = yield* Database.query(Filter.type(types['com.example.type.task'])).run;\nyield* print('total tasks', all.length);\nconst docs = all.filter(t => typeof t.title === 'string' && t.title.toLowerCase().includes('docs'));\nyield* print('docs-matching', JSON.stringify(docs.map(t => ({ id: t.id, title: t.title, status: t.status }))));\n"},"providerExecuted":false}]},{"options":{},"role":"tool","content":[{"options":{},"type":"tool-result","id":"toolu_01EvQkZjnZybkdPD9rVppr7A","name":"eval","isFailure":false,"result":{"output":"total tasks 3\ndocs-matching [{\"id\":\"01JGFJJZ00G0WKQSJGMAKCNTS7\",\"title\":\"Write the docs\",\"status\":\"open\"}]"},"providerExecuted":false}]},{"options":{},"role":"assistant","content":[{"options":{},"type":"reasoning","text":"With only 3 tasks total, I want to double-check each title against the \"mentions docs\" criterion before finalizing.\n\n"},{"options":{},"type":"text","text":"Only one literal \"docs\" match, but let me check the other titles before deciding."},{"options":{},"type":"tool-call","id":"toolu_01Qv88bq8659GTV1yc8TmxwR","name":"eval","params":{"code":"const all = yield* Database.query(Filter.type(types['com.exa